Compressed textures of any size on Windows 10. Applied by installer/tools/assemble_payload.py to the payload's copy of the
toolkit; the checked-out repository is not edited.
DXT1/23/45 textures whose width or height is not a multiple of 4 can't be created as block-compressed resources by Windows
10's D3D12 runtime (CreateCommittedResource fails, debug-layer message 597; Windows 11 allows them). J-Stars' menus use
512x78 DXT5 pieces, so a tester on Windows 10 saw menus without art, entries or text. Those textures are now
decoded to RGBA8 on the CPU, on every machine, so everyone sees the same image; BC_NATIVE=1 keeps them compressed (test).
Tested on Windows 11: the main menu logs four 512x78 textures decoded and looks as before, with no debug-layer
errors.
